WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:04.020
In a land where it is always
winter and never Christmas,

2
00:00:04.070 --> 00:00:06.490
a boy betrays his family.

3
00:00:06.540 --> 00:00:10.340
A great lion offers his own
life in the boy's place.

4
00:00:10.390 --> 00:00:14.130
At sunrise, the Stone Table cracks.

5
00:00:14.180 --> 00:00:15.060
The writer, C.

6
00:00:15.110 --> 00:00:15.280
S.

7
00:00:15.330 --> 00:00:17.920
Lewis, was an atheist as a young man.

8
00:00:17.970 --> 00:00:23.380
So why would a story about a lion and
a witch be read as a story about Jesus?

9
00:00:23.430 --> 00:00:28.400
In this mission, you'll explore Narnia,
and a stranger book about a bus ride from

10
00:00:28.450 --> 00:00:29.850
a grey town.

11
00:00:29.900 --> 00:00:35.500
Then you'll compare fiction, non-fiction
and poetry as ways of expressing belief.

12
00:00:35.550 --> 00:00:40.800
Your mission: find out how a story about
a lion and a witch can be read as a story

13
00:00:40.850 --> 00:00:41.950
about Jesus.
